1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,617
You download a hundred and nine megabytes.
About twenty-six of it is the game.

2
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:06,976
The rest is the engine carrying it.

3
00:00:09,226 --> 00:00:14,653
Disco Ball Simulator 2000.
You owe a million dollars and you own one disco ball.

4
00:00:14,903 --> 00:00:19,154
So you swipe it, over and over,
until the party pays it off.

5
00:00:19,404 --> 00:00:24,857
A hundred and forty-six DLLs.
Eighty megabytes. Three quarters of the download.

6
00:00:25,107 --> 00:00:30,194
And the biggest file that isn't a
DLL is Unity's own default resources.

7
00:00:30,594 --> 00:00:35,916
That isn't a criticism. It's the floor —
what a small game costs on a big engine.

8
00:00:36,316 --> 00:00:40,332
Worth a dip. Every demo I open,
I read the file list first.
